  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many pictures of 6 megabytes each can be stored on Pete's memory card, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total capacity of the memory card in megabytes.\n2. Determine how many 6-megabyte pictures can fit into the total capacity of the memory card.\n\nFirst, we calculate the total capacity of the memory card. The memory card can hold 3,000 pictures of 8 megabytes each. Therefore, the total capacity in megabytes is:\n\\[\n3000 \\times 8 = 24000 \\text{ megabytes}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find out how many 6-megabyte pictures can fit into 24000 megabytes. We do this by dividing the total capacity by the size of each picture:\n\\[\n24000 \\div 6 = 4000\n\\]\n\nSo, the memory card can hold \\(\\boxed{4000}\\) pictures of 6 megabytes each.",
